# What is Docker
Docker is an open-source platform used to
develop, package, and run applications inside containers

A container is a lightweight, standalone environment that includes:
Application code
Libraries
Dependencies
Runtime
This ensures the application runs consistently across different systems

❌ Without Docker
To run a Node.js app:
Install Node.js
Install dependencies
Match versions
👉 May fail on another system

✅ With Docker
docker run node-app
✔ Docker automatically:
Sets up environment
Installs dependencies
Runs application

🎯 Why Docker is Important
Consistency across environments
Faster deployment
Lightweight and efficient
Eliminates “it works on my machine” problem


