# Why Docker
Docker is used to package, ship, and run applications in a consistent and efficient way using containers.

“Docker solves dependency and environment issues by packaging applications into containers, making them portable, lightweight, and easy to deploy compared to traditional virtual machines.”

Portability – Run the same app anywhere (local, server, cloud)
Consistency – Same environment → no errors across systems
Lightweight – Uses fewer resources than virtual machines
Fast Execution – Containers start in seconds
Isolation – Apps run independently without conflicts
Easy Deployment – Build once, deploy anywhere


