# Containers vs Virtual Machines (Simple)
Containers and Virtual Machines are used to run applications in isolated environments.

A Virtual Machine (VM) runs a full operating system along with the application. It needs more memory and takes more time to start because each VM has its own OS.

A Container runs the application with its dependencies but shares the host system’s OS. It is lightweight, uses fewer resources, and starts quickly.

Containers are faster and more efficient, while Virtual Machines are heavier but provide full system isolation.


